 "sentences": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 9.3,
   "n_words": 31,
   "text": "He drilled 82 holes into the wood, because down the hill, an army is marching straight for his fort, and while everyone else sharpens swords, he's in the corner still drilling."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.46,
   "end": 12.4,
   "n_words": 10,
   "text": "His commander asks, are we fighting them or grating cheese?"
  },
  {
   "start": 12.8,
   "end": 13.84,
   "n_words": 4,
   "text": "But it gets weirder."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.02,
   "end": 20.12,
   "n_words": 23,
   "text": "He bolts the wood onto a cart, and into every hole goes something long and thin, wrapped in paper, each with a string."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.38,
   "end": 24.02,
   "n_words": 13,
   "text": "Then he twists all the strings into one rope nobody's allowed to touch."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.24,
   "end": 28.5,
   "n_words": 17,
   "text": "One soldier reaches for it, and he slaps his hand so hard the whole fort hears it."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.5,
   "end": 29.94,
   "n_words": 4,
   "text": "That night, it pours."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.14,
   "end": 33.86,
   "n_words": 18,
   "text": "So he throws his coat over the cart and lies on top of it like a human umbrella."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.14,
   "end": 36.32,
   "n_words": 9,
   "text": "One drop gets in there, and we're all dead."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.54,
   "end": 39.94,
   "n_words": 12,
   "text": "The next morning, ladders slam against the walls and the army charges."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.28,
   "end": 47.84,
   "n_words": 28,
   "text": "Everyone screams at him to do something, but he just watches them get closer and closer, until they're packed shoulder to shoulder, close enough to see their teeth."
  },
  {
   "start": 48.12,
   "end": 50.42,
   "n_words": 11,
   "text": "That's when he rips off the coat and lights the rope."
  },
  {
   "start": 50.58,
   "end": 59.52,
   "n_words": 31,
   "text": "The spark races down it and splits into 82 tiny flames, and each one hits a tube of gunpowder strapped to an arrow, turning every one of them into a rocket."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.84,
   "end": 63.28,
   "n_words": 12,
   "text": "All 82 blast off the cart at once, flying every which way."
  },
  {
   "start": 63.42,
   "end": 66.46,
   "n_words": 12,
   "text": "But with the army packed that tight, not a single one misses."
  }
 ]
}